oss":"retirou","count":1},{"gloss":"partiu","count":1}]},"G3406":{"id":"G3406","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3406","disambiguated_id":"G3406 =","unique_id":"G3406","headword":"μισθαποδότης","transliteration":"misthapodotēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"rewarder","definition_en":"μισθ-απο-δότης, -ου, ὁ \n (see supr.), \none who pays wages; meton., a rewarder: Heb.11:6.†\n (AS)","source_line":3519}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"buscam","count":1}]},"G3701":{"id":"G3701","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3701","disambiguated_id":"G3701 =","unique_id":"G3701","headword":"ὀπτασία","transliteration":"optasia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"vision","definition_en":"ὀπτασία, -ας, ἡ\n (ὀπτάζομαι, Num.14:14* = ὀπτάνομαι), later form of ὄψις, [in LXX: Mal.3:2 (רָאָה ni.), Da TH Dan.9:23 10:1, 7-8 10:16 (מַרְאֶה, מַרְאָה LXX, ὅραμα, -σις), Est.4:7, Sir.43:2, 16 * ;] \n__1. an appearing, coming into view (Ma, Es, Sir, ll. with). \n __2. a vision: Luk.1:22 24:23, Act.26:19, 2Co.12:1 (Da, ll. with, also in MGr.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3817}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"visão","count":2},{"gloss":"aparição","count":1},{"gloss":"visões","count":1}]},"G3890":{"id":"G3890","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3890","disambiguated_id":"G3890 =","unique_id":"G3890","headword":"παραμύθιον","transliteration":"paramuthion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"comfort","definition_en":"παραμύθιον, -ου, τό\n (παραμυθέομαι) [in LXX: Wis.3:18 * ;] \n__1. an exhortation, persuasion, encouragement: Php.2:1 (cf. Plat., Legg., vi, 773 E, al.; see Lft. and ICC, Phi., l.with). \n __2. assuagement, abatement, hence, consolation (Wis, l.with, and frequently in cl.).†\n (AS)","source_line":4008}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"conforto","count":1}]},"G4301":{"id":"G4301","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4301","disambiguated_id":"G4301 =","unique_id":"G4301","headword":"προλαμβάνω","transliteration":"prolambanō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to take beforehand","definition_en":"προ-λαμβάνω \n [in LXX: Wis.17:11 א2, Wis.17:17 א2B * ;] \n__1. to take beforehand: with accusative, 1Co.11:21 (but see infr.). \n __2. to be beforehand, anticipate (in cl., with accusative, genitive or dative): with inf. (= cl. φθάνω, see Bl., § 69, 4; Swete, in l), Mrk.14:8. \n __3. to overtake, surprise: pass., Gal.6:1 (on the virtual disappearance of the temporal force of the preposi­tion in this compound here and perhaps also in 1Co, l.with, see MM, xxi).†\n (AS)","source_line":4431}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"podia","count":2},{"gloss":"surpreendido","count":1}]},"G4363":{"id":"G4363","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4363","disambiguated_id":"G4363 =","unique_id":"G4363","headword":"προσπίπτω","transliteration":"prospiptō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to fall/beat","definition_en":"προσ-πίπτω\n [in LXX for נָפַל, נָגַע hi., כָּרַע ;] \n__1. to fall upon, strike against: with dative, of wind, Mat.7:25. \n __2. to fall down at one's feet, fall prostrate before: absol., before πρός, Mrk.7:25; with dative of person(s), Mrk.3:11 5:33, Luk.8:28, Act.16:29; τ. γόνασιν, Luk.5:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":4493}],"occurrence_count":8,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"prostrou-diante","count":3},{"gloss":"prostrou","count":2},{"gloss":"atingiram","count":1},{"gloss":"prostravam-se-diante","count":1},{"gloss":"prostrou-se-diante","count":1}]},"G4596":{"id":"G4596","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4596","disambiguated_id":"G4596 =","unique_id":"G4596","headword":"σηρικός","transliteration":"sērikos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"silk","definition_en":"σιρικός (by assimilation of vowels, for σηρικός; see Mayser, 150; WH, Notes, 151), -ή, -όν \n (οἱ Σῆρες, a people of India from whom the ancients got the first silk), \nsilk, silken; as subst., τὸ σ., silken fabric, silk: Rev.18:12 (cf. FlJ, B.J., vii, 5, 4).†\n (AS)","source_line":4734}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"seda","count":1}]},"G4721":{"id":"G4721","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4721","disambiguated_id":"G4721 =","unique_id":"G4721","headword":"στέγη","transliteration":"stegē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"roof","definition_en":"στέγη, -ης, ἡ\n (στέγω) [in LXX: Gen.8:13 (מְכַסֶּה), etc. ;] \na roof: Mrk.2:4; of entering a house, εἰσέρχεσθαι ὑπὸ τὴν σ., Mat.8:8, Luk.7:6 (cf. MM, xxiii).†\n (AS)","source_line":4869}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"telhado","count":2},{"gloss":"teto","count":1}]},"G4788":{"id":"G4788","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4788","disambiguated_id":"G4788 =","unique_id":"G4788","headword":"συγκλείω","transliteration":"sugkleiō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to confine","definition_en":"συν-κλείω\n (Rec. συγκ-), [in LXX chiefly for סגר ;] \nto shut together, enclose, shut in on all sides: of a catch of fish, Luk.5:6; metaphorically (Psa.31:9, al.), Rom.11:32, Gal.3:22-23.†\n (AS)","source_line":4936}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"recolheram","count":2},{"gloss":"prendeu","count":1},{"gloss":"encerrados","count":1}]},"G5108":{"id":"G5108","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5108","disambiguated_id":"G5108 =","unique_id":"G5108","headword":"τοιοῦτος","transliteration":"toioutos","lexical_morphology":"G:D","gloss_en":"such as this","definition_en":"τοιοῦτος, -αύτη, -οῦτο\n (as usually in Att.. prose. Ep. and Ion. neut. -οῦτον in Al., Act.21:25, Rec. only), \ncorrelat. of οἷος, ὁποῖος, ὥς, etc., \n such as this, of such a kind, such: Mat.9:8 18:5, Mrk.4:33 6:2 7:13 9:37 (T, τούτων), Jhn.9:16, Act.16:24, 1Co.5:1 11:16, 2Co.3:4 3:12 12:3, Heb.7:26 8:1 12:3 13:16, Jas.4:16; οἷος . . . τ., 1Co.15:48, 2Co.10:11; id. pleonast. (see Bl., § 50, 4), Mrk.13:19; before ὁποῖος, Act.26:29; ὥς, Phm 9. As sub